<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaabu Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kaabu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kaabu Empire was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Mandinka</a> state in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea-bissau">Guinea-Bissau</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-gambia">The Gambia</a>. It emerged in the thirteenth century as an outlying province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> and later became independent. It has its own profile on the site and fell in the nineteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire.jpg" alt="Kaabu Empire" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Duke of liang · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaabu_18th_Century_Map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
